From 362b3243eee65b6f1fc78f6339d2893d958df725 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 17:36:02 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 07/12] rpc,doc: say that a node's own transactions reveal
 their origin

Nucleation relay removed the random announcement delays, and a node sends
the transactions it originated (wallet, RPC: the unbroadcast set) to every
relay peer at the next tick (since the fan-out commit), so a fraction of
transactions does not die at a source whose few chosen peers do not relay
it on. Both make the entry node of a transaction easy to see: in the relay
simulation a 10% spy set finds the origin of 75-90% of node-originated
transactions. As decided, privacy is to come from the client instead:
submitting each transaction through several independent nodes.

The sendrawtransaction and submitrawtxbatch help now say so, and the
release notes describe the new relay and its settings. Sending through
several nodes from the wallet PWA is a separate task in that project (not
a daemon change).

Tests: rpc_help.py and rpc_rawtransaction.py pass; test/lint/check-doc.py
passes. That originated transactions go to every peer is tested in
p2p_tx_relay_fanout.py and txrelay_tests (fan-out commit).
---
 doc/release-notes.md | 21 +++++++++++++++++++++
 src/rpc/mempool.cpp  | 10 +++++++++-
 2 files changed, 30 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/doc/release-notes.md b/doc/release-notes.md
index aaf9b65f2c..23c1d2fa9e 100644
--- a/doc/release-notes.md
+++ b/doc/release-notes.md
@@ -36,3 +36,24 @@ This release includes the following features and fixes:
   and the `logging` RPC but has no effect; it is deprecated. A host name given
   to the command line client's `-rpcconnect` is now tried on each of its
   addresses, and `-rpcclienttimeout=0` now means no timeout at all.
+
+Nucleation transaction relay
+----------------------------
+
+Transaction relay no longer delays announcements randomly. Every peer is
+sent announcements on one fixed tick (`-txrelaytick`, default 10 ms). A
+relayed transaction is announced to a fan-out of peers,
+clamp(max(min, ceil(pct x relay peers)), min, max) (`-txrelayfanoutmin` 8,
+`-txrelayfanoutpct` 0.25, `-txrelayfanoutmax` 32); a transaction this node
+originated (wallet, RPC) goes to every peer at the next tick. Peers that
+negotiate it (`sendinvshort`) receive 8-byte short ids (`invshort`,
+`-txrelayshortids`) and reconcile recently admitted transactions every
+`-txreconinterval` (250 ms) over a `-txreconwindow` (30 s); other peers keep
+receiving ordinary `inv` messages. Unsolicited bodies to high-bandwidth
+peers now need `-txrelaypushhb=1`. Announcements per peer are capped by
+`-txrelayratemax` (250,000 per second).
+
+Privacy: relay timing no longer hides which node a transaction entered the
+network at, and a node's own transactions go to all of its peers at once.
+Wallets that care should submit each transaction to several independent
+nodes (`sendrawtransaction` on each).
diff --git a/src/rpc/mempool.cpp b/src/rpc/mempool.cpp
index eab7529f5e..444ccdfedd 100644
--- a/src/rpc/mempool.cpp
+++ b/src/rpc/mempool.cpp
@@ -50,6 +50,10 @@ static RPCHelpMan sendrawtransaction() {
         "sendrawtransaction",
         "Submits raw transaction (serialized, hex-encoded) to local node and "
         "network.\n"
+        "\nThe node announces transactions it originated to all of its "
+        "peers at the next relay tick, without delay, so peers can tell "
+        "which node they came from. For privacy, submit each transaction to "
+        "several independent nodes rather than to one.\n"
         "\nAlso see createrawtransaction and "
         "signrawtransactionwithkey calls.\n",
         {
@@ -1566,7 +1570,11 @@ static RPCHelpMan submitrawtxbatch() {
         "no transactions in the batch are accepted.\n"
         "Phase 2 commits all validated transactions to the mempool under the "
         "same cs_main lock acquisition, refreshes the RCU snapshot, and "
-        "broadcasts them.\n",
+        "broadcasts them.\n"
+        "\nThe node announces transactions it originated to all of its "
+        "peers at the next relay tick, without delay, so peers can tell "
+        "which node they came from. For privacy, submit each transaction to "
+        "several independent nodes rather than to one.\n",
         {
             {
                 "rawtxs",
